{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"6b0cad4578a7a29a270d281c0e921d6cc2c9d28837874d8e77301fadf1a0ea03","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar.toml project configuration","key_entities":["rebar.toml","[verify] section","verify.overlap_enabled","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/","src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py","_store/event_append.py","_store/push.py","[tool.rebar.llm] overlap_drain*","tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py","tests/unit/test_plan_review_overlap.py","rebar review-plan","REBAR_LLM_OVERLAP_DRAIN"],"problem_keywords":["overlap detection","config flag","plan-review","enrichment drain","activation"],"propositions":["The cross-ticket overlap detector (epic-crave-art) code is shipped and tested but gated off by default; verify.overlap_enabled must be set to true in rebar.toml to activate store-wide overlap detection.","Enabling verify.overlap_enabled=true activates two code paths: plan-review overlap step (advisory, populates overlap[] on verdict) and opportunistic enrichment drain (asynchronously builds BM25F digests, fires on ticket writes).","The enrichment drain is best-effort and cannot fail writes; it is bounded by overlap_drain* tunables and independently disableable via [tool.rebar.llm] overlap_drain='off'.","Enabling the flag broke 7 tests in test_enrich_drain.py because write-path drain calls with repo_root=None read ambient checkout config, causing auto-drain pollution; fix pins REBAR_LLM_OVERLAP_DRAIN=off in the module's repo fixture.","The config change must be verified by: rebar.toml parsing, load_config() reading the flag as true, rebar review-plan outputting JSON with 'overlap' key present, and all tests passing."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785822727445594791,"uuid":"1e17a540-cae6-4330-bff8-bc3f903eb1f6"}